; Regression: `&c` on a MUTABLE reference cell is one wrapper deeper — the
; other half of xfail_address_of_ref_type.scaly (2026-08-28).
;
; `&` is the identity only where there is no slot to address. A `var` of
; reference type HAS one, the emitter answers that slot (`ret %r`), and the
; type must say so — this is the shape every out-cell in the tree is built on
; (`fill(&cell)` against a `ref[ref[X]?]` parameter), so getting the identity
; rule too wide would silently flatten all 51 of them.
;
; xfail: ref[ref[Box]] where int is declared

define Box (v: i64)

function f(b: ref[Box]) returns int
{
    var c: ref[Box] b
    let n: int &c
    n
}

Console.println "`f`"
